}

// THE GAPS ARE FOUR ENTRIES AND SEVEN FOLD SITES, AND THEY ARE CARRIED RATHER THAN ROUNDED AWAY.
//
// None of the four holds an `empty_map()` site, so the spelling this row was filed under is measured
// end to end; the residue is in the widened frame only. Three of the four refuse at emit with a named
// diagnostic and one is killed by host memory, which are different facts with different fixes -- a
// refusal is a corpus or emitter question, a kill is a machine question -- so they are separate
// variants rather than one "not measured" bucket. Reporting 1 of 179 measured sites as though it were
// 1 of 186 would be the narrow this row exists to avoid.
//
// THE EMITTER IS NOT BUILT FROM THE SUBJECT, and the row says so in a field rather than in prose that
// a later reader can skip. The DIRECTION matters and was checked rather than assumed: the emitter's
// commit is fifteen minutes NEWER than the measured tree and sits on no main ancestry, reachable only
// from one session branch. So this is not a stale-instrument risk -- the worry is not that an old
// emitter missed sites a current one would produce. It is that an off-main emitter may carry emission
// behaviour main does not, which makes the measured population the population THAT emitter produces.
//
// WHAT THE CONTROLS DO AND DO NOT LICENSE. The instrument reproduced the known site exactly, and
// sixteen further E0282 sites in the same output are assigned elsewhere by the partition key, so the
// key can answer no. Together those establish that the instrument DETECTS this class -- a mechanism.
// They do not establish that the population is complete, because a control never can. The honest
// reading is mechanism-confirmed, population conditional on this emitter.

// WHY THIS IS ITS OWN ROW RATHER THAN A NOTE ON THE ROW THAT SURFACED IT.
//
// It was found inside gunbc.lambda_argument_typing_gate's three-site partition and stays listed there
// as a member, because that partition records how the three were derived TOGETHER and splitting it
// would destroy the only artifact of that derivation. But the CAUSE is distinct, the repair is
// distinct, and it belongs to neither the String declaration-site work nor the bare-name roster the
// partition was originally filed under. A cause with its own repair earns its own row; a site does
// not stop being a member of the set it was found in.
data untyped_fold_init_surfaced_by: DeclarationRef = decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.lambda_argument_typing_gate", decl_name: "lambda_typing_gate_sites")

// DISSOLUTION IS KEYED TO THE SITE COMPILING, NOT TO ANY PARTICULAR REPAIR. The sibling row learned
// this the expensive way: its first trigger named a mechanism, that mechanism turned out to be inert,
// and the trigger was therefore satisfiable by a change that fixed nothing -- a false trigger
// disposes of the evidence, which is worse than a false cause misleading a reader.
data untyped_fold_init_dissolution_trigger: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "dissolve-on: every site in untyped_fold_init_sites emits an initial accumulator whose type is determined without a caller-supplied annotation, and compiles with no inference-failure diagnostic at that position, established by execution against the emitted crate. Not satisfied by annotating the closure parameter at the call site -- that moves the obligation to the author rather than deriving it, and the .dag source already carries the accumulator's type at the fold's declared signature. The basis is now SweptCorpus, so a green on the listed site retires the class ACROSS THE SWEPT FRAME -- 56 of the 60 in-frame files, 179 of the 186 in-frame fold sites. It does not retire the four entries in coverage_gaps, whose 7 fold sites were never measured; those close by re-running the sweep's emit and check over them, not by anything that happens at the listed site.")
